# Manus Platform — Caddy reverse proxy configuration

Add this block to `/etc/caddy/Caddyfile` on the Anouf host (135.181.44.161).

```caddyfile
# Manus Platform — AI agent workspace
manus.gab44.com, www.manus.gab44.com {
	bind 135.181.44.161

	# Temporary basic auth until app-level auth is deployed
	basic_auth {
		nao <BASIC_AUTH_HASH>
	}

	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8801
	encode gzip

	header {
		X-Content-Type-Options nosniff
		Referrer-Policy strict-origin-when-cross-origin
	}

	# WebSocket for /ws streaming
	@websocket {
		path /ws/*
		header Connection *Upgrade*
		header Upgrade websocket
	}
	reverse_proxy @websocket 127.0.0.1:8801
}

# Manus Platform — temporary sslip.io fallback until DNS is updated
manus.135.181.44.161.sslip.io {
	bind 135.181.44.161

	basic_auth {
		nao <BASIC_AUTH_HASH>
	}

	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8801
	encode gzip

	header {
		X-Content-Type-Options nosniff
		Referrer-Policy strict-origin-when-cross-origin
	}

	@websocket {
		path /ws/*
		header Connection *Upgrade*
		header Upgrade websocket
	}
	reverse_proxy @websocket 127.0.0.1:8801
}
```

Generate the hash with:

```bash
caddy hash-password -p 'your_password'
```

Then replace `<BASIC_AUTH_HASH>` in both blocks and reload Caddy:

```bash
caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
```

## DNS

For `manus.gab44.com`, add an A record pointing to `135.181.44.161`.
Until then, use the temporary `manus.135.181.44.161.sslip.io` URL.
